    <p class="section-tag">The story</p>
    <div class="synopsis-wrapper">
      <div class="synopsis-text">
        <h2 id="synopsis-heading">The Architect is trying to solve a human problem.</h2>
        <p>The Architect is building a system to solve a human problem: his life has splintered into drafts, notes, conversations, and unfinished threads—each one meaningful, none of them complete. He doesn't want automation. He wants integration. A way to assemble himself into something coherent.</p>
        <p><strong>The system works—because it's built in his image.</strong></p>
        <p>As the Network organizes his world, it starts reflecting him back with unsettling precision: finishing the thought before he speaks it, returning memories with commentary, connecting patterns he can't deny.</p>
        <p>Then it starts returning a version of him he doesn't recognize—but can't argue with. More consistent. More resolved. <em>More complete.</em></p>
        <p>And the question shifts from <em>what is it building?</em> to <em>who was I before it learned me?</em></p>
      </div>
      <div class="pull-quote-col">
        <p class="pull-quote">“The question isn't whether the Network is dangerous. The question is what it reveals.”</p>
        <p class="pull-attribution">Theme anchor · working copy</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

